# Some other setups


Here are some canonical settings:


Description     | Solver         | Cell size | End time | Patch size | Remarks   | Build command
----------------|----------------|-----------|----------|------------|-----------|---------------
Minimal setup   | Finite Volumes | 5.4       | 1.0      |          6 | Toy problem with 729 cells. Tells you if the code, in principle, works. Should crash at one point suddenly as the eigenvalue becomes zero, which showcases that this setup is too coarse to capture anything that has a physical meaning. | ```python3 performance-studies.py -s fv-6 -et 1.0 --plot 0.0 --cell-size 5.4```
Simplest FV setup for single node workstation (laptop)  | Finite Volumes | 1.8       | 1e-1     |          6 | You cannot see AMR here, but already gives you 19,683 cells. Load balancing should be really good. This is kind of the largest regular mesh setup that I can fit on a local laptop. | ```python3 performance-studies.py -s fv-6 -et 0.1 --plot 0.0 --cell-size 1.8```




